  40:./ucos/Core/os_time.c **** *
  41:./ucos/Core/os_time.c **** * Description: This function is called to delay execution of the currently running task until the
  42:./ucos/Core/os_time.c **** *              specified number of system ticks expires.  This, of course, directly equates to dela
  43:./ucos/Core/os_time.c **** *              the current task for some time to expire.  No delay will result If the specified del
  44:./ucos/Core/os_time.c **** *              0.  If the specified delay is greater than 0 then, a context switch will result.
  45:./ucos/Core/os_time.c **** *
  46:./ucos/Core/os_time.c **** * Arguments  : ticks     is the time delay that the task will be suspended in number of clock 'tick
  47:./ucos/Core/os_time.c **** *                        Note that by specifying 0, the task will not be delayed.
  48:./ucos/Core/os_time.c **** *
  49:./ucos/Core/os_time.c **** * Returns    : none
  50:./ucos/Core/os_time.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
  51:./ucos/Core/os_time.c **** */
